        <p>The top row is the publishing path: source files in a Git repository, built and validated by Vercel on every push to <code>main</code>, served from Vercel's edge. The bottom row is what a browser pulls in at runtime besides the pages themselves. Media never passes through Git or the build—it is uploaded straight to R2 and referenced by filename, so a site rebuild never has to move a gigabyte of audio.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section alt" id="hosting">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Hosting, domains and delivery</h2>

        <table class="uth-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Concern</th><th scope="col">How it is handled</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Page hosting</th><td>Vercel, configured as a plain static output (<code>framework: null</code>, output folder <code>_site</code>). Pages are served from Vercel's edge cache.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Canonical address</th><td><code>https://www.wordsofplainness.org</code>. The bare domain, <code>brotheraaron.org</code> (with and without <code>www</code>) and the default <code>*.vercel.app</code> address all answer with a permanent 301 to the canonical host, so search engines see one site.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Media</th><td>A separate subdomain, <code>media.wordsofplainness.org</code>, fronts a Cloudflare R2 bucket. Audio and banner images are fetched from there directly by the browser; banner images carry long-lived immutable cache headers.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Transport</th><td>HTTPS only, with HSTS (two-year max-age) and Brotli compression on HTML.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Caching</th><td>HTML is sent <code>max-age=0, must-revalidate</code> but held at the edge, so a deploy is visible immediately while repeat visits are still served from cache.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Retired URLs</th><td>A short list of redirects in <code>vercel.json</code> keeps old chapter slugs and moved pages working.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Companion app</th><td><em>Keep My Commandments</em> lives at <code>commandments.brotheraaron.org</code>, a separately hosted Django application rather than part of this static build.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>There is no service worker and no offline mode; the site is meant to be read online, and keeping it a set of ordinary documents is what lets it work in unusual browsers such as the desktop browsers used inside VR headsets.</p>
    </div>
</section>

